.venv/
# Dashboard runtime state (composite-runs.db + WAL/SHM, dashboard/, runs/,
# viz-requests/, agent-responses/, …). Everything under .pbg/ is generated;
# the directory is recreated on demand by the dashboard. v2ecoli friction
# #15 (2026-05-19): a granular per-subdir list missed sqlite WAL/SHM
# sidecars (.pbg/composite-runs.db-shm / -wal) and .pbg/dashboard/, which
# tripped the dashboard's own dirty-tree gate on Install + workstream
# commit. Note: `.pbg/*` (not `.pbg/`) so the re-include below can rescue
# scaffolded schema files — gitignore can't re-include children of a
# parent directory that's been fully excluded.
.pbg/*
# .pbg/schemas/*.json (workspace/study/investigation) ship via scaffold
# and ARE authored content. They live under .pbg/ for namespacing but
# need to remain tracked.
!.pbg/schemas/
# hpc.env.example is a committed template; hpc.env and hpc_known_hosts
# are gitignored by .pbg/* above (they hold real credentials/key paths).
!.pbg/hpc.env.example
# Investigation runtime artifacts (results DB + rendered HTML + lock file).
# spec.yaml + data/ are tracked; everything else is regenerated on each run.
investigations/*/runs.db
investigations/*/viz/
investigations/*/.run.lock
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
# Dashboard-copied report assets (style.css, client.js, vivarium-logo.png, …) —
# regenerated from vivarium-workbench on each report render. Only .keep is tracked.
workspace/reports/assets/*
!workspace/reports/assets/.keep
# Transient brainstorm session artifacts (server PIDs, logs, rendered HTML).
.superpowers/brainstorm/
